g"],[1444,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[1582,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[1579,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[1577,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[1587,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1475,"✅ Custom domains"],[1476,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1209,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1360,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. Undo / Redo, Zoom In / Out / Reset)"],[1359,"✅ For grouped contextual actions — two or more closely related actions that belong together (e.g. Bold / Italic / Underline, Align Left / Center / Right)"],[1361,"✅ For multi-select scenarios — when users need to select multiple options simultaneously"],[245,"✅ For selecting multiple independent options"],[1208,"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"],[247,"✅ For toggling settings or features on/off"],[1474,"✅ Interactive tooltips"],[1473,"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"],[1471,"✅ Single and multi-series support"],[1472,"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"],[248,"✅ When all available options should be visible"],[984,"✅ When all options should be visible at once"],[985,"✅ When the decision is important and deserves space"],[983,"✅ When there are 2-7 mutually exclusive options"],[246,"✅ When users can select zero, one, or many items"],[987,"❌ For binary yes/no choices (use Checkbox or Tog